&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SonarQube documentation, project analysis and webhooks: &lt;a href="https://docs.sonarsource.com/sonarqube-server/latest/analyzing-source-code/overview/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://docs.sonarsource.com/sonarqube-server/latest/analyzing-source-code/overview/&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ZoomEye documentation: &lt;a href="https://www.zoomeye.org/doc" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://www.zoomeye.org/doc&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a submission for the &lt;a href="https://dev.to/challenges/hacktoberfest-week3-2026-10-19"&gt;Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge Week 3: Slow and Steady&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What I Built
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fridge-to-Feast&lt;/strong&gt; is a zero-effort, local-first recipe visualizer specifically designed for exhausted, busy, or unapologetically lazy home cooks who adhere to a &lt;strong&gt;100% pure vegetarian diet&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of staring into an open fridge with decision fatigue—or giving up on home cooking because washing 5 greasy pots feels like a mountain of labor—Fridge-to-Feast turns random ingredients into an instant, satisfying feast with &lt;strong&gt;minimal physical effort&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Dual-Input Fridge Intake&lt;/strong&gt;: Snap and drop a quick shelf photo, or type scattered ingredients (&lt;code&gt;"Potatoes, Tomatoes, Coriander"&lt;/code&gt;), or tap 1-click pantry staple chips.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Sloth Cooking Energy Slider&lt;/strong&gt;: Select how much effort you can spare:

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⚡ &lt;strong&gt;Microwave Chef (3 mins)&lt;/strong&gt;: Zero pan watching, zero chopping, single mug or bowl.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🍳 &lt;strong&gt;One-Pan Stir-Fry (15 mins)&lt;/strong&gt;: Quick sizzle, light dice, maximum flavor-to-effort ratio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🍲 &lt;strong&gt;Slow Simmer (30 mins)&lt;/strong&gt;: Low-heat stew or curry—walk away and take a nap while it simmers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;"Minimize Dishes" 1-Vessel Lock&lt;/strong&gt;: Automatically adapts every recipe to a &lt;strong&gt;single mug, skillet, or pot&lt;/strong&gt;, eliminating cutting boards and prep bowls so cleanup takes 15 seconds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;"Lazy Substitutions" (Zero-Store Swaps)&lt;/strong&gt;: Missing an ingredient? Don't leave your couch. Tap any pantry alternative (e.g., swapping &lt;em&gt;Paneer&lt;/em&gt; with &lt;em&gt;Tofu&lt;/em&gt; or &lt;em&gt;Boiled Chickpeas&lt;/em&gt;, or &lt;em&gt;Butter&lt;/em&gt; with &lt;em&gt;Ghee + Salt&lt;/em&gt;). The cooking steps dynamically rephrase so instructions match how the swap actually behaves in the pan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;🦥 "Sloth Nap" Hands-Free Cooking Timer&lt;/strong&gt;: Synced to your recipe duration with soothing Web Speech voice announcements (&lt;em&gt;"Wake up, master... your feast is ready..."&lt;/em&gt;) and real-time synthesized pentatonic chimes so you can rest your eyes without burning dinner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




